WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.492
The fourth condition counts distinct medications for each patient.

00:00:03.492 --> 00:00:07.247
COUNT DISTINCT returns one scalar value for the current patient.

00:00:07.247 --> 00:00:11.837
Run the query and identify which patients have more than one distinct medication.

00:00:11.837 --> 00:00:16.497
Now all four pieces of the final practice query have been tested independently.

00:00:16.497 --> 00:00:20.242
For this activity, make a prediction before you run anything.

00:00:20.242 --> 00:00:24.922
State what one output row should represent, which records you expect to remain,

00:00:24.922 --> 00:00:28.082
and what edge case is most likely to expose a mistake.

00:00:28.082 --> 00:00:31.737
Then run the SQL and compare the result with that prediction.

00:00:31.737 --> 00:00:37.742
If it does not match, debug the logic in small pieces instead of changing several clauses at once.

00:00:37.742 --> 00:00:43.382
This is the same habit you would use in a real analytics project: validate the meaning of the result,

00:00:43.382 --> 00:00:45.417
not only whether the statement executes.
